    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **289 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature: when an owner is created, the response now includes an integer field `namesakeCount` counting how many other owners already shared the same last name at that moment.\n\nChanges made, following the existing conventions used for `membershipNumber`/`customerCode`/`membershipTier`:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `namesakeCount` read-only integer property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and MapStruct maps it automatically).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `namesake_count` column field with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Before saving, counts existing owners with a matching last name and sets it on the new owner.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column so the value persists and is returned on the later `GET /api/owners/{id}` that the acceptance test reads back.\n\nIt's persisted (not just set on the response) because the acceptance test creates the owner, then reads the value back via `GET`, which loads a fresh entity from the database.",
